tools.description:
Permanently deletes the webhook and its subscriptions. This cannot be undone.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/version_1/manage/delete-webhook/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/v1/{id}

Removes one subscription without deleting the webhook.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/version_1/subscriptions/delete-subscription/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/v1/{id}/subscriptions/{subscription_id}

Some forecast outputs are calculated after the underlying forecast data becomes available. This endpoint lets you check when degree day (HDD/CDD) and tropical cyclone calculations are available for each model initialization time, as well as which calculations are still in progress or incomplete.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/forecasts/version_1/forecast-availability/calculation_times/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/forecasts/v1/{model}/calculation_times/{calculation_type}

Return one event's summary, geometries, and forecast-hour details for the selected initialization. See About Weather Events for details about event detection, tracking, and severity.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/insights/version_1/events/event-detail/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/insights/v1/wm-6/{event_id}

Return events of the requested type for one model initialization, including each event's summary and geometries. Atmospheric rivers, heatwaves, and coldwaves have polygon footprints and severity regions; fronts have line geometries. See About Weather Events for details about event detection, tracking, and severity.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/insights/version_1/events/events/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/insights/v1/wm-6/{event_type}

Retrieve the complete vertical profile data for a specific atmospheric sounding collected by WindBorne's balloon constellation. This endpoint returns detailed measurements at multiple altitude levels including temperature, humidity, pressure, and wind data.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/observations/version_1/soundings/sounding/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/observations/v1/soundings/{sounding_id}

Fetch all available data for a model's tropical cyclone for its latest or a requested initialization time. Use an operational ATCF ID or a generated ID returned by the index. See About the Tropical Cyclone Tracker for details about paths, landfalls, cones, and storm identification.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/forecasts/version_1/tropical-cyclones/tropical-cyclone-detail/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/forecasts/v1/wm-6/tropical_cyclones/{tc_id}

Retrieve the full details of a single webhook, including its configuration and all subscriptions.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/version_1/manage/get-webhook/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/v1/{id}

Update the core properties of a webhook. This endpoint accepts both PATCH and PUT.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/version_1/manage/update-webhook/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/v1/{id}

Update a single subscription on a webhook. This endpoint accepts both PATCH and PUT. The request body is partial, so omitted fields remain unchanged. Use get_webhook first when the subscription type is unknown. degree_days.available: This subscription is sent after the degree day calculation for a model run has completed. The payload identifies the matching model run whose population-weighted HDD and CDD forecasts are available. events.available: Receive a notification when atmospheric river, heatwave, coldwave, and front products are published for a model run and can be queried through the Events API. By default, one notification waits for all four types from the same initialization. Subscribe to specific types to receive their notifications independently, without waiting for the others. Each notification covers a complete forecast, not one individual event or forecast hour. forecast_hour.available: This subscription sends a notification for each individual forecast output as it becomes available. The payload includes the model, initialization time, forecast zero, forecast hour, and the time at which the forecast is valid. initialization_time.available: The forecast cycle is complete when every expected forecast hour for a model run is available. The payload includes the model, initialization time, and forecast zero. tropical_cyclones.available: This subscription is sent once tropical cyclone forecasts have been published for a matching model run. The payload includes the model, initialization time, forecast zero, and tropical cyclone IDs even when no response option is configured.

Documentation: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/version_1/subscriptions/update-subscription/

Default endpoint: https://api.windbornesystems.com/webhooks/v1/{id}/subscriptions/{subscription_id}
